<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Barmstedt</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Barmstedt is a small town in the Pinneberg district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schleswig-holstein">Schleswig-Holstein</a>, north-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamburg">Hamburg</a>. In 1649 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christian-rantzau">Christian Rantzau</a> bought the district from the Duke of Holstein-Gottorp, and in 1650 it became the imperial County of Rantzau, governed from a castle on an island in the Rantzau lake. After the county was seized in 1726 it came under Danish administration.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/barmstedt.jpg" alt="Barmstedt" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: PodracerHH at German Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Blick_zur_Kirche.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
